IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-art01-03`
IMPORT `epd-art05-06`
IMPORT `epd-art13`
IMPORT `epd-art14-21`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), Publications Office consolidated version of 19.12.2009 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF THE SENDER.
--
-- SEAT: a person or business that sends direct marketing by automatic calling machine, fax, electronic mail or another means (the
-- "sender"): one sender, one recipient, one message or call at a time.
--
-- This layer phrases the layer-1 modules (epd-art05-06, epd-art13, epd-art14-21 ...) as the questions the sender asks. It restates no rule:
-- every question calls one layer-1 function with every argument named, from plain inputs worded as the sender is asked. The individual's
-- seat (epd-seat.l4) and the provider's seat (epd-seat-provider.l4) are separate layers over the same modules; the recipient's
-- questions about the same message call the same layer-1 functions, so the two seats cannot disagree (the mirror cases, epd-cases-seat-mirror.l4).
-- There is no seat for an authority or a court: their powers appear only as what they mean for the sender
-- ("Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop?", "Do the judicial remedies and sanctions apply against me?").
--
-- A DIRECTIVE BINDS MEMBER STATES, NOT PEOPLE. Where the text says "Member States shall take appropriate measures to ensure that ... are
-- not allowed", the answer says what the DIRECTIVE requires the national law to do; it does not say what any one Member State's law says,
-- or whether a provision has direct effect (NOTES.md). A sender is bound by its Member State's transposing law, which is not in the sources.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE = the text says yes. JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words. NOTHING = the text does not
-- answer (silent, self-limited, list not closed, or pointing outside the sources). NOTHING is not "no" (NOTES.md, "Reading a result:
-- FALSE and NOTHING"). For the whole-message question, JUST TRUE = the message may be sent; JUST FALSE = the text says it may not.
--
-- Borrowed terms (the data subject's consent, direct marketing, personal data and the terms Article 2 takes from Directives 95/46/EC
-- and 2002/21/EC) are facts the sender states; so is the national option under Art 13(3), which national legislation chooses and the
-- sources do not state.

§ `ePrivacy Directive -- the sender's questions`

§§ `May I send this message? (Article 13)`
-- The sender asks about one message and one recipient. The recipient's seat (epd-seat.l4) asks the same questions from the other side.

-- The whole-Article answer, put together in layer 1 from paragraphs 1 to 5. JUST TRUE = the message may be sent; JUST FALSE = the text says it may not; NOTHING = the text does not answer.
@export May I send this marketing message to this recipient (Art 13)?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `my message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `the recipient did not ask for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message unsolicited (the recipient did not ask for it)?
      `the recipient is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
      `the recipient consented beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the recipient give consent before the message was sent?
      `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the recipient's electronic contact details from the recipient as your customer?
      `I got them in the context of a sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in the context of the sale of a product or a service?
      `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
      `I am the same person that got the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the same natural or legal person that obtained the details?
      `I am marketing my own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the marketing of your own products or services?
      `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products or services similar to those you sold to the customer?
      `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you clearly and distinctly give the customer the opportunity to object to this use of the details?
      `the offer to object was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that opportunity free of charge?
      `the offer to object was easy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in an easy manner?
      `I offered it when I collected the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it at the time the details were collected?
      `the recipient initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the customer initially refuse such use?
      `I offered it with each message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it on the occasion of each message?
      `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent?
      `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message contravene Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC?
      `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message have no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease?
      `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message encourage recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article?
      `national law has chosen` IS A `Article 13(3) national option` @desc For a message that is not an automatic call, fax or e-mail: has national legislation chosen that such messages need the recipient's consent, or that people who do not wish to receive them are protected? One of: consent of the subscriber or user is required, subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected, national legislation has not been stated.
      `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the recipient not wish to receive these messages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I send this marketing message to this recipient` IS
    `Art 13 the message may be sent to the recipient` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `my message is for direct marketing`
        `the message is unsolicited` IS `the recipient did not ask for it`
        `the recipient is a natural person` IS `the recipient is a natural person`
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `the recipient consented beforehand`
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer`
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `I got them in the context of a sale`
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `I am the same person that got the details`
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `I am marketing my own products or services`
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `they are similar to what the recipient bought`
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object`
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the offer to object was free`
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the offer to object was easy`
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `I offered it when I collected the details`
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS `the recipient initially refused such use`
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `I offered it with each message`
        `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS `my message disguises or conceals who I am`
        `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC`
        `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS `my message has no valid address for requests to stop`
        `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article`
        `option` IS `national law has chosen`
        `the recipient does not wish to receive these communications` IS `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages`

@export Has the recipient's prior consent made this use of the means allowed (Art 13(1))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `my message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `the recipient consented beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the recipient give consent before the message was sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the recipients prior consent made this use of the means allowed` IS
    `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `my message is for direct marketing`
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `the recipient consented beforehand`

@export Is this the kind of use Art 13(1) names (Art 13(1))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `my message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this the kind of use Article 13(1) names` IS
    `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `my message is for direct marketing`

@export Does the existing-customer exception cover this message (Art 13(2))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the recipient's electronic contact details from the recipient as your customer?
      `I got them in the context of a sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in the context of the sale of a product or a service?
      `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
      `I am the same person that got the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the same natural or legal person that obtained the details?
      `I am marketing my own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the marketing of your own products or services?
      `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products or services similar to those you sold to the customer?
      `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you clearly and distinctly give the customer the opportunity to object to this use of the details?
      `the offer to object was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that opportunity free of charge?
      `the offer to object was easy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in an easy manner?
      `I offered it when I collected the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it at the time the details were collected?
      `the recipient initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the customer initially refuse such use?
      `I offered it with each message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it on the occasion of each message?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the existing customer exception cover this message` IS
    `Art 13(2) the soft opt-in applies` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer`
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `I got them in the context of a sale`
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `I am the same person that got the details`
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `I am marketing my own products or services`
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `they are similar to what the recipient bought`
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object`
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the offer to object was free`
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the offer to object was easy`
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `I offered it when I collected the details`
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS `the recipient initially refused such use`
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `I offered it with each message`

@export May I use this means given the recipient's consent or the existing-customer exception (Art 13(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `my message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `the recipient consented beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the recipient give consent before the message was sent?
      `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the recipient's electronic contact details from the recipient as your customer?
      `I got them in the context of a sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in the context of the sale of a product or a service?
      `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
      `I am the same person that got the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the same natural or legal person that obtained the details?
      `I am marketing my own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the marketing of your own products or services?
      `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products or services similar to those you sold to the customer?
      `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you clearly and distinctly give the customer the opportunity to object to this use of the details?
      `the offer to object was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that opportunity free of charge?
      `the offer to object was easy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in an easy manner?
      `I offered it when I collected the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it at the time the details were collected?
      `the recipient initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the customer initially refuse such use?
      `I offered it with each message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it on the occasion of each message?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I use this means given consent or the existing customer exception` IS
    `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `my message is for direct marketing`
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `the recipient consented beforehand`
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer`
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `I got them in the context of a sale`
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `I am the same person that got the details`
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `I am marketing my own products or services`
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `they are similar to what the recipient bought`
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object`
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the offer to object was free`
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the offer to object was easy`
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `I offered it when I collected the details`
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS `the recipient initially refused such use`
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `I offered it with each message`

§§ `Other unsolicited marketing, and what is prohibited in any event (Article 13(3) and (4))`

@export Does Art 13(3) apply to this call or message (Art 13(3))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the recipient did not ask for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication unsolicited?
      `it is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purposes of direct marketing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Article 13(3) apply to this call or message` IS
    `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the communication is unsolicited` IS `the recipient did not ask for it`
        `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `it is for direct marketing`

-- JUST TRUE = the Directive requires the national law to make it not allowed.
@export Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message (Art 13(3))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the recipient did not ask for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication unsolicited?
      `it is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `national law has chosen` IS A `Article 13(3) national option` @desc For a message that is not an automatic call, fax or e-mail: has national legislation chosen that such messages need the recipient's consent, or that people who do not wish to receive them are protected? One of: consent of the subscriber or user is required, subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected, national legislation has not been stated.
      `the recipient consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the recipient consent to it?
      `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the recipient not wish to receive it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` IS
    `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the communication is unsolicited` IS `the recipient did not ask for it`
        `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `it is for direct marketing`
        `option` IS `national law has chosen`
        `the subscriber or user has consented` IS `the recipient consented`
        `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` IS `the recipient does not wish to receive it`

@export Is the option national law chose free of charge for the recipient, as Art 13(3) requires?
GIVEN `the option is free of charge for the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the option national law chose free of charge for the recipient?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national option free of charge for the recipient as Article 13(3) requires` IS
    `Art 13(3) the option is free of charge for the subscriber or user` WITH
        `the option the national legislation chose is free of charge for the subscriber or user` IS `the option is free of charge for the recipient`

@export Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event (Art 13(4))?
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How are you sending it? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `my message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent?
      `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message contravene Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC?
      `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message have no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease?
      `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message encourage recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event` IS
    `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` WITH
        `means` IS `how I send it`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `my message is for direct marketing`
        `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS `my message disguises or conceals who I am`
        `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC`
        `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS `my message has no valid address for requests to stop`
        `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article`

@export Do paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to this recipient as a natural person (Art 13(5))?
GIVEN `the recipient is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to this recipient as a natural person` IS
    `Art 13(5) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to the subscriber` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `the recipient is a natural person`

@export The recipient is a company: must its legitimate interests be sufficiently protected (Art 13(5))?
GIVEN `the recipient is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `The recipient is a company: must its legitimate interests be sufficiently protected` IS
    `Art 13(5) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `the recipient is a natural person`

§§ `Being taken to court, ordered to stop, or penalised (Articles 13(6), 15, 15a)`
-- Only for a sender that has been, or may be, the subject of a complaint, a court action or an authority's order.

@export May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `the person is adversely affected by the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person adversely affected by an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13?
      `the person has a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement?
      `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message` IS
    `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` WITH
        `the person is adversely affected by an infringement of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS `the person is adversely affected by the infringement`
        `the person has a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement` IS `the person has a legitimate interest in stopping it`
        `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests` IS `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests`

@export If someone sues me, can the authority still act against me administratively (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does national law provide an administrative remedy (for example an order to stop) under Article 15a(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If someone sues me can the authority still act against me administratively` IS
    `Art 13(6) the legal proceedings leave the administrative remedy unaffected` WITH
        `there is an administrative remedy for which provision is made under Article 15a(2)` IS `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)`

@export Must my Member State have penalties for this infringement (Art 15a(1))?
GIVEN `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my Member State have penalties for this infringement` IS
    `Art 15a(1) first sentence the Member State must lay down rules on penalties applicable to the infringement` WITH
        `the infringement is of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive`

@export May a penalty cover the whole period of a breach I have since put right (Art 15a(1))?
GIVEN `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the penalty applied to cover the period of the breach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a penalty cover the whole period of a breach I have since put right` IS
    `Art 15a(1) second sentence the penalty may be applied to cover the period of the breach, even if the breach has been rectified` WITH
        `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach` IS `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body the power to order the cessation. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop (Art 15a(2))?
GIVEN `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive?
      `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the power?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop` IS
    `Art 15a(2) the body must have the power to order the cessation of the infringement` WITH
        `the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive`
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the power` IS `it is relevant for that body to have the power`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body that power. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me, as a sender, to give it information when it investigates (Art 15a(3))?
GIVEN `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a sender to give it information when it investigates` IS
    `Art 15a(3) the body must have the investigative powers and resources, including the power to obtain information` WITH
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources` IS `it is relevant for that body to have the powers`

@export Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95/46/EC apply against me (Art 15(2))?
GIVEN `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter concern national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive?
      `it concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern an individual right derived from this Directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95 46 EC apply against me` IS
    `Art 15(2) Chapter III of Directive 95/46/EC on judicial remedies, liability and sanctions applies` WITH
        `the matter concerns national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive`
        `the matter concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS `it concerns an individual right derived from this Directive`

§§ `Is it electronic mail, is it consent, and what I put on the recipient's device (Articles 2 and 5)`

@export Is my message "electronic mail" under the Directive (Art 2(h))?
GIVEN `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message a text, voice, sound or image message?
      `I send it over a public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent over a public communications network?
      `it can be stored until the recipient collects it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until collected?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my message electronic mail under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` WITH
        `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS `it is a text, voice, sound or image message`
        `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS `I send it over a public communications network`
        `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS `it can be stored until the recipient collects it`

@export Is what the recipient did "consent" under the Directive (Art 2(f))?
GIVEN `what the recipient did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what the recipient did count as the data subject's consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC (freely given, specific and informed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what the recipient did consent under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(f) the act of the user or subscriber is consent` WITH
        `the act of the user or subscriber is the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC` IS `what the recipient did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC`

@export Do I need consent to store information on the recipient's device or read it (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `I store information on the recipient's device or read what is on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your message or service store information in the recipient's terminal equipment, or gain access to information already stored there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need consent to store information on the recipients device or read it` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the storing or access is only allowed on condition of consent` WITH
        `the act is the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user` IS `I store information on the recipient's device or read what is on it`

@export Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on, or read from, the recipient's device (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `the recipient gave consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the recipient give consent?
      `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give clear and comprehensive information, including about the purposes?
      `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the consent and information in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from the recipients device` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH
        `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS `the recipient gave consent`
        `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS `I gave clear and comprehensive information`
        `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC`
